,title,link,text,language,family
0,Suba-Simbiti language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suba-Simbiti_language,"Suba-Simbiti is spoken by six groups in the Tarime region of Tanzania. This include Hacha, Kine, Sweta, Simbiti and Kiroba. The total number of speakers is in the region of 110,000.",Suba-Simbiti,Niger-Congo
1,Suba-Simbiti | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/ssc/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..I_2nPeShi1OaWGAnY2DTMoWnSEb6GHb7JAZGxPMSCgU,Suba-Simbiti is a stable indigenous language of Tanzania. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family.,Suba-Simbiti,Niger-Congo
2,Suba-Simbiti – TIPs,https://tips.translation.bible/tip_language/ssc/,"Niger-Congo > Atlantic-Congo > Volta-Congo > ...Suba-Simbiti: “Whenever you have just small faith, [even] if it were like a small mustard seed, you would tell this fig tree thus, ‘Uproot, you should go, you should be planted in the lake!’ and it would obey you.”",Suba-Simbiti,Niger-Congo
3,Suba-Simbiti - ssc (Niger-Congo) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/ssc/,"People Groups who primarily speak Suba-Simbiti. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page. Visualize lostness with powerful maps.",Suba-Simbiti,Niger-Congo
4,Suba-Simbiti in Tanzania people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/index.php/people_groups/18960/TZ,"The Suba-Simbiti are a Bantu ethnic group living in the Mara Region of northwestern Tanzania, particularly in the Tarime, Musoma Rural, and Musoma Urban districts. They are composed of six closely related subgroups: Hacha, Kine, Kiroba, Surwa, Sweta, and Simbiti.",Suba-Simbiti,Niger-Congo
5,Suba language Facts for Kids,https://kids.kiddle.co/Suba_language,JE.403 (shared w Suba-Simbiti). The Suba language is spoken by the Suba people in east Africa.Bantu languages are a major branch of the Niger-Congo language family. They are known for having similar grammar rules and words.,Suba-Simbiti,Niger-Congo
6,"Suba-Simbiti language. Evangelism tools, church planting resources...",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/ssc,Suba-Simbiti language and dialect information. Audio Bible stories and lessons.Suba-Simbiti. Work with GRN on this language. Are you passionate about Jesus and communicating the Christian gospel to those who have never heard the Bible message in their heart language?,Suba-Simbiti,Niger-Congo
7,Suba people (Tanzania),https://grokipedia.com/page/suba_people_tanzania,"The Suba people of Tanzania, also known as the Suba-Simbiti, are a Bantu ethnic group primarily inhabiting the Mara Region in northwestern Tanzania, along the eastern shores of Lake Victoria.",Suba-Simbiti,Niger-Congo
